1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,141
Question six.

2
00:00:01,141 --> 00:00:06,583
Step one: macro scan. It asks what a 40-to-250 height rule is.

3
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:10,445
One mark. Command words: “this practice is”.

4
00:00:10,445 --> 00:00:12,025
Step two: denoise.

5
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:17,818
Useful, in yellow: height, forty to two hundred fifty centimetres.

6
00:00:17,818 --> 00:00:21,329
In cyan: “must be between” — the bounds.

7
00:00:21,329 --> 00:00:26,069
Useless red herring: the clinic setting — kick it out.

8
00:00:26,069 --> 00:00:27,649
Step three: draft.

9
00:00:27,649 --> 00:00:32,038
There are bounds; the system checks automatically.

10
00:00:32,038 --> 00:00:35,374
Automatic rule checking is validation.

11
00:00:35,374 --> 00:00:37,831
Not double-entry comparison.

12
00:00:37,831 --> 00:00:39,323
Step four: P O E.

13
00:00:39,323 --> 00:00:43,537
A, verification: confused with validation — cut.

14
00:00:43,537 --> 00:00:47,048
B, encryption: secrecy, off-topic — cut.

15
00:00:47,048 --> 00:00:50,120
C, backup: copies, off-topic — cut.

16
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:57,054
Step five: sanity check and lock. A range rule is validation, not verification.

17
00:00:57,054 --> 00:00:59,424
So the correct answer is D.

